<Layout title="Tipping by Country | International Tip Guide" description="A planned guide to tipping customs by country, with room for researched country guidance and a future interactive map."><ContentPage eyebrow="Travel planning" title="Tipping by country" intro="Tipping customs vary by country, venue, and service. This page is the foundation for researched country-by-country guidance; the interactive map will be added once the data is verified."><h2>Why local context matters</h2><p>A percentage that feels normal in one place may be unnecessary or confusing somewhere else. Look for service charges, read the menu or bill, and ask a trusted local source when the custom is unclear.</p><h2>Planned country guide</h2><p>Future entries will distinguish between expected, appreciated, and unusual tipping. Each entry will explain restaurant, taxi, hotel, and personal-service context where reliable sources support it.</p><div class="country-status"><strong>Research-ready structure</strong><p>Country cards and an interactive map will be added here after current local guidance has been checked. No country rankings or unsupported universal rules are presented.</p></div><h2>Until then</h2><p>Use the <a href="/how-much-to-tip">how much to tip guide</a> for general context, and check with your accommodation or venue while travelling.</p></ContentPage></Layout>
